      "body": "## Overview\n\nThe DeepSeek V3.1 tool parser dropped any text that came after a tool-calls block on the non-streaming path. Streaming already returned that text. This is the same gap as #56263. #56265 covers the V3 parser only. This change is the V3.1 parser, which is a separate file and still registered as `deepseek_v31`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `extract_tool_calls` returns the text before the tool-calls block plus the text after `tool_calls_end`.\n- A missing end marker keeps the old behavior: prefix only.\n- Tool names and arguments are unchanged.\n- Streaming is not modified.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe non-streaming cases were run here with a tiny in-memory tokenizer: prefix only, prefix plus suffix, and suffix only. All three returned the expected content and tool names. `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` passed on the two files.\n\nThe existing unit tests download `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.1` and were not run on this machine. Importing vLLM here fails before the tokenizer step.\n\n```bash\npytest tests/tool_parsers/test_deepseekv31_tool_parser.py\n```\n\n## Details\n\n`extract_tool_calls` used to slice at the start marker and ignore the rest. Streaming emits a content delta once the tool-call start and end counts match again, so the text after the block reaches the client only on the streaming path.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
